  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Chad Acute Joint Response</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The war in Sudan has caused an influx of 585.000 new refugees reaching Chad in one year. People are facing critical living conditions in different camps in the four eastern provinces, adding to existing harsh conditions and pressure on available resources for host communities. One of these camps is Arkoum camp in Ouaddai province, established April 2023 with 20,000 people and now recently more than doubled to 50,506 people.

Arkoum has been chosen for implementation by Tearfund in consultation with LM. For WASH interventions LM is partnering with ATALNA (Association Tarikh Al Nadjana). The choice for Arkoum was based on the high level of needs and the existing presence of LM and ATALNA enabling a quick scale up in addressing new WASH needs.</narrative>
  </description>
